Leptos components styled after shadcn/ui, driven by shadcn-format CSS themes.

Third-party material:

  shadcn/ui (https://github.com/shadcn-ui/ui), MIT, Copyright (c) 2023 shadcn.
    The design: token names, the radius scale, component sizes and states, and
    the default "neutral" theme (themes/neutral.css) follow shadcn/ui's source.
    Full text: LICENSES/shadcn-ui-MIT.txt

  gpui-component (https://github.com/longbridge/gpui-component), Apache-2.0,
  Copyright 2024 - 2026 Longbridge.
    The Indicator component (a count or dot marker overlaid on an element) is
    derived from gpui-component's Badge: its geometry and behaviour. The crate
    was first built from gpui-component's component specs before moving to
    shadcn/ui; no gpui-component themes or colour code remain.
    Full text: LICENSES/gpui-component-Apache-2.0.txt
    Changes: rewritten for Leptos and the DOM, styled with CSS custom properties.

  Lucide (https://lucide.dev), ISC, Copyright (c) for portions of Lucide are held by
  Cole Bemis 2013-2022 as part of Feather (MIT); all other copyright (c) Lucide Contributors 2022.
    The shapes of the public icon set (src/icon_name.rs, generated by scripts/gen-icons.py
    from lucide-static 0.468.0) and the glyphs components draw themselves.
    Full text: LICENSES/lucide-ISC.txt

  Leptix UI (https://github.com/RantAI-dev/leptix-ui), MIT, Copyright (c) 2025 Rantai Dev <dev@rantai.dev>.
    The headless primitives in src/primitives/ are ported from Leptix and extended.
    Taken at commit ac8f006870520e821aa436b96f285ccb57b82d41 (2026-04-03, v0.1.6).
    Full text: LICENSES/LEPTIX-MIT.txt
    Leptix is itself a Rust port of the Radix UI primitives (https://www.radix-ui.com,
    MIT, Copyright (c) 2022 WorkOS). Behavior and API shape follow Radix.
    Changes: the separate leptix-* crates are merged into one module tree, `leptix_core`
    becomes `primitives::core`, and each primitive is one module next to it. Names and
    paths changed; behavior is unchanged unless a commit says otherwise. Upstream's
    core/collection.rs and core/roving_focus.rs were not ported: they are never declared
    in upstream's lib.rs, do not compile, and reference crates upstream does not depend on
    (nanoid, radix_leptos_primitive). Upstream is no longer tracked; this is now our code
    to maintain.
